Description: build the Lua bytecode without luajit's -d option
 bcc 0.35 compiles bcc.lua with 'luajit -bgd'. The -d (deterministic
 bytecode) option only exists in LuaJIT releases from 2024 on; noble ships
 2.1.0+git20231223, which rejects it and prints its usage text. Dropping -d
 only gives up byte-for-byte reproducible bytecode.
Forwarded: not-needed

--- a/src/lua/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/src/lua/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -15,7 +15,7 @@
 
 	ADD_CUSTOM_COMMAND(
 		OUTPUT bcc.o
-		COMMAND ${LUAJIT} -bgd bcc.lua bcc.o
+		COMMAND ${LUAJIT} -bg bcc.lua bcc.o
 		DEPENDS bcc.lua
 	)
 
